  "control_definitions": {
    "bulk": "Optimize B2/fcc reservoirs and calculate both vacancies in 2x2x2 and 3x3x3 supercells with matched reciprocal density.",
    "surface": "For each of Ni-terminated(100), Al-terminated(100), mixed(110), compare species exchanges with central layers and vacancy/adatom transfer cycles. Record layer identities and all atom counts.",
    "convergence": "Use 7- and 9-layer slabs and 15/20 angstrom vacuum starts; these define checks, not promised convergence. Converge representative slab k mesh/energy cutoff.",
    "phase": "Calculate relaxed L12 Ni3Al and the common-reservoir grand potential. Check elemental precipitation constraints; if Ni3Al changes the allowed equilibrium reservoir window, report B2 metastability rather than silently using inconsistent equilibrium chemical potentials.",
    "surface_symmetry": "For nonstoichiometric terminations include chemical-potential terms and surface multiplicity; a two-face asymmetric slab energy is not a single termination energy."
  },
  "observable_definition": "Ni-rich mu_Ni=E(fcc Ni)/atom and mu_Al=E(B2 NiAl)/formula_unit-mu_Ni. E_vac(X)=E(defect)-E(pristine)+mu_X. Atom-conserving E_seg=E(exchanged slab)-E(clean slab). Balanced transfer E_tr(X)=E(bulk V_X)+E(slab+X)-E(bulk)-E(slab). Ni3Al grand potential per formula unit=E(L12 Ni3Al)-3mu_Ni-mu_Al. Use the same converged Hamiltonian/reservoirs throughout.",
  "experimental_conditions": {},
